source hito: HITO's own choice, not taken from a code

H-15
  use: plain concrete only (simples, sin armar)
    Verified, cirsoc-201-2005: 2.3.2, Tabla 2.7 (p. Cap. 2 - 38)
  compressive strength: 15 MPa (SI 15000000.0)
    Verified, cirsoc-201-2005: 2.3.2, Tabla 2.7 (p. Cap. 2 - 38)
  young modulus: 18,203 MPa (SI 18203000000.0)
    Derived, cirsoc-201-2005: 8.5.1, expresión (8-1): Ec = 4700 √f'c, in MPa (p. Cap. 8 - 187); rounded to 1 MPa
  unit weight: 23.5 kN/m³ (SI 23500.0)
    Assumption, cirsoc-101-2005: Tabla 3.1, Hormigones: hormigón de cemento pórtland, arena y canto rodado o piedra partida, sin armar (p. Cap. 3 - 6)
    note: The value is verified. H-15 is for unreinforced concrete only (Tabla 2.7), so the unreinforced row applies. Choosing the row for natural gravel or crushed stone (not basaltic, 25 kN/m³) is HITO's choice.
  mass density: 2,396 kg/m³ (SI 2396.0)
    Derived, cirsoc-101-2005: unit weight ÷ standard gravity (9.80665 m/s²), so self-weight is exactly the code's unit weight; rounded to 1 kg/m³
  shading colour: #c8c8c8
    Assumption, hito: a grey that darkens as the strength grows

